# DESIGN-RETRO — reasoning wave (compact retro block per agent at finale)

## background retro
**Load-bearing decision**: background tasks are injected as `{_bg: true}` nodes BETWEEN foreground steps, never replacing them; cadence interrupts are non-blocking annotations when no break window exists. This preserves greedy's ordering invariant.
**New primitives required**: `bg{}` descriptor on step nodes; `backgroundTask`/`cadenceMinutes`/`lifecycleState` on GuideStep; `weaveBackground()` post-pass in greedy.js; `_bg_step()` in enrich.py.
**Deliberately left to synthesizer**: (1) shared "break" tag definition across all facets; (2) `est_minutes` field on steps (needed by background + likely others); (3) inventory budget arbitration when bg injects mid-slayer; (4) courier task cadence (speculative — must measure live).
**Synthesizer MUST NOT MISS**: agility marks are yield annotations, NOT background tasks (pattern 6 embed, not cadence loop); kitten feeding is annotation-only, not a hard interrupt; slayer-seed hook wires pattern 8 into pattern 4 at planner level — this virtuous cycle is the heart of mid-game self-sufficiency; supply_threshold_jit is the bridge from ahead-of-time scheduling to JIT escalation (402:138 bias in data reflects this asymmetry).

## steer retro
**Load-bearing decision:** anchor_weight float (0–1) on each steer-point drives whether it
becomes a hard phase boundary (>= 0.8), soft boundary (0.5–0.79), or inline waypoint (<0.5).
This single scalar keeps the phase-count manageable without hard-coding every diary/unlock.
Ardougne Easy Diary gets anchor_weight 1.0 — the canonical pattern-12 anchor from retros.

**Deliberately left to synthesizer:**
- Whether steer_points.jsonl is a separate file or an extension of goals.jsonl (OQ-1).
- VARBIT/VARPLAYER condition type for access-unlock auto-detection (OQ-2).
- STEER_HARD_THRESHOLD constant publication shared with interleave facet (OQ-3).
- Recurring-loop lifecycle representation (birdhouses, herb runs) — steer marks recurring:true; interleave facet owns the cadence steps (OQ-4).

**Synthesizer MUST NOT miss:**
- steer_id foreign key on steps.jsonl nodes is the ONLY link from planner steps to steer-points; if omitted, phased_steps_with_steer() cannot group steps by steer intent.
- supply_infra steer-points depend on supply facet step definitions; synthesizer must reconcile so neither facet double-defines the underlying steps.
- pet-drop steer-points have anchor_weight 0.0 — they must appear in catalog (completeness) but never emit as phase boundaries.

## sequencer retro
**Load-bearing decision:** Keep background/passive steps entirely out of the greedy heap;
inject them post-hoc via injectSlots(). Mixing them into the heap would let them consume
priority slots away from goal-critical steps and corrupt the greedy's cost ordering.
**Deliberately left to synthesizer:**
- Authoring the background step bank (herb runs, birdhouses, seaweed) — sequencer only models
  the slot schema; content is supply-chain facet's domain.
- RECURRING completionCondition type in GuideStep — render facet must implement the timer.
- Phase-naming registry — four facets will emit phase strings; need a shared contract.
- AVG_STEP_MIN calibration — all background cadence timing is placeholder until measured.
**Synthesizer MUST NOT MISS:**
- OQ-5: hub_batches must run before topo_order, not after, to avoid dep-order violations.
- OQ-4: deferred_until conflicts with supply-chain demand — needs explicit priority rule.
- The `RECURRING` condition type lands between sequencer and render; assign it explicitly.

## burndown retro
**Load-bearing decision**: Items are NOT separate entities — they are edge weights on
step→step dependency arcs. The `produces/consumes` fields on steps.jsonl encode supply
chains without a new data tier. This keeps greedy.js extensible without a schema overhaul.

**Resolution algorithm key move**: Cycle detection via VISITED set + bootstrap break.
The herblore/herb-farming cycle is the canonical example; resolved by emitting a
one-time low-tier gather before the loop is established. This is a general pattern for
all self-feeding supply chains.

**Left to synthesizer**: (1) Rate placeholders — decide config-file vs inline tooltip.
(2) Background loop slot assignment — the interleaving facet must define the contract
with loop:true steps. (3) Priority order for authoring the 28 stub coarse expansions.
(4) Confirm Catherby charter pineapple source is still valid in current game.

**Synthesizer MUST NOT MISS**:
- RFD Pirate Pete is minigame-locked — no supply staging, breaks the general pattern.
- The `reqs.items` goal field must not silently fail in greedy.js before burndown.js wires in.
- Bootstrap gather steps (one-time, pre-loop) must be ordered BEFORE loop setup in topo_order.
- Stew RNG steps need explicit player-facing rate uncertainty — do NOT fabricate attempt counts.

## synthesis retro
**The model in one paragraph**: A progression is a requisite burndown interleaved by one
pipeline: burndown.js resolves goal item/quest reqs into gathered/produced roots (item math
internal, bridged to greedy as tags + a demandSet); greedy routes ACTIVE steps only
(slot-typed background/passive excluded; deferred_until holds breakpoint-trained skills
unless demandSet overrides — hard requisites beat soft deferrals); weaveOverlays injects
background setups/cadence chips/passive badges/alternation markers as _anchor-pinned nodes;
enrich hub-batches BEFORE topo (topo is the dep guard), places supply steps by timing,
re-pins overlays, and phases everything on steer-point anchors (anchor_weight >=0.8 hard),
with phase_name() the sole author of phase strings and all unknown rates "??"/tuning
placeholders.
**Riskiest reconciliation**: S6 — routing item quantities around greedy entirely (tag-bridge
+ demandSet instead of numeric item state), because coalesce is max-semantics and reqs.items
is silently ignored today; if the tag-bridge under-specifies quantities, plans pass greedy
yet under-supply the goal — burndown.js execution-count math is the only guard.
**FIRST lane**: Lane 1 — steer_points.jsonl (6 nodes) + steer_id on ~8 steps +
bg-farm-allotment row + new overlay.js/tuning.js + 3-line greedy bank split + enrich
phase_name()/steer emitters; web view shows steer phases + bg chips; zero Java churn.

