## feasibility-gate retro (2026-07-14, route-grand 60→0 faults)
Load-bearing decision: 47/60 checker faults were MODEL artifacts, not route faults — route_feasibility.mjs
now folds quest-reward XP (graph.js effectiveLevel parity; ba2ce570 prunes bands quest XP covers, so the
pruned band can never grant the plain floor), credits quests by kind/tag (rfd-* rows), credits bankless
synth-* bands via their SKILL completionConditions, and class-matches reqs.items ("prayer_potion" ~
"prayer_potion_4"). The 13 real faults were all one root bug + one missing contract:
  (1) isinstance(True, int) is True in Python — topo_order/phased_steps/phased_steps_with_steer/
      _coalesce_checkpoints all dispatched numeric grants BEFORE `v is True`, so EVERY boolean tag grant
      ({"has-volcanic-ash": true}) became a level-1 "skill" and the S7 tag-bridge was silently unenforced
      in the re-simulations; tag-gated supply cores always fell to the unordered tail dump. bool-first now.
  (2) P10 phased_steps had no demand model: goal.demand_gate (grand-only opt-in) adds §2-epoch supply
      demand-hold (chain held until the episode of the first milestone whose reqs.tags demands
      supply-<chain>), chain-registry queue + scaffolding pairwise-wait (withdraws sit adjacent to their
      gated cores), reqs.items class gate (unlock-barrows/gwd wait for brew/cook), ordered endgame drain,
      P10a/P10b anchor-pin round-trip (opp/bg nodes ride around the re-pick; their grants/produces still
      enter P10 state at the anchor), and _pin_prefix stamps (origin prefix owns the route opening).
Deferred: route-corpus keeps 3 item faults (region-phased appendix, no milestone episodes → demand_gate
does not apply); plan-multi/plan-corpus order-only diffs (id-sets equal) are the tag-bridge finally
enforcing — intentional re-bakes, npm 93/93 both before and after.
MUST-NOT-MISS: any new re-simulation that applies grants MUST dispatch `v is True` before isinstance
int/float; route_feasibility.mjs is the standing 0-fault gate for ordering work on the grand spine.

## state-consolidation retro (2026-07-14, state_scan.mjs + state_after on all 372 steps)
Load-bearing decision: state_after is a SIMULATOR output, not authored content, so it can cover the
whole route mechanically instead of needing the "prefix to full depth, brief the rest" fallback the
task offered — state_scan.mjs (sibling to route_feasibility.mjs, refactored to export its bank/xp/
skill engine behind an `isMain` guard so both tools share one source of truth) extends the existing
{skills,quests,unlocks} accumulator with inv/worn/bank Maps driven by atom{}.verb transitions
(withdraw/deposit/equip specially; every other verb — or no atom{} at all, most coarse rows — falls
back to the row's own top-level produces{}/consumes{}). Values touched by any "??" placeholder are
marked `approx` and rendered by NAME ONLY, never a fabricated count — same "??"-over-guesses rule as
everywhere else, just applied to a Map instead of a JSON field. Wired through the SAME sidecar/attach
pattern as methods[]/subChecklist (state_after.jsonl -> enrich.py extra_by_id merge, gated on new
goal.state_after opt-in, plan-grand.mjs only) — verified a fixed point: state_scan run against the
freshly re-baked route reproduces byte-identical sidecar content (it reads only the requisite bank,
never its own prior output), and a second full rebake reproduces byte-identical route JSON.
Result: 372/372 steps carry state_after; 0 slot-overflow flags; 3 loadout-placeholder steps (the
prayer-pot-supply pps-01/03/05 withdraw atoms) are flagged as a documented LOWER BOUND on slot count
since their itemized contents live only in prose `detail`, never structured data — a real Lane-5 gap
(the withdraw atoms should eventually carry an itemized consumes{}), not a state_scan bug.
route_feasibility.mjs itself gained real coverage during this pass: steps_origin.jsonl (the
character-creation/Tutorial-Island ori-t-* prefix, ~24 rows) was never in its BANKS join, so those
steps silently fell into the bankless/synthetic fallback the whole time — added it (in-bank coverage
316->339/372), still 0 faults (all origin rows are reqs:{} in practice).
Heap-scan (order_audit.mjs, new tool): computed readyAt (first position a bank step's reqs clear,
valid because state only accumulates — feasibility=0 already proves this) vs takenAt for every bank
step; 206 candidates with gap>=20. IMPORTANT CAVEAT for whoever reads this next: route_feasibility's
0-fault invariant means NONE of these 206 are correctness violations by construction (a dependency can
never be scheduled after its dependent, or feasibility would fault) — the gap metric measures SLACK,
not bugs. Triage: the ~144 QoL/unlock gaps are dominated by trivial-reqs quests (ready@0) that the P10
milestone-episode/demand_gate machinery deliberately clusters into the episode of the goal that needs
them rather than front-loading in isolation — WORKING AS INTENDED (avoids fragmenting the route into
one-off detours, serves the proximity criterion better than max-front-loading would). The pps-*
supply-chain gaps (pps-01..06, 281-302) are the documented demand_gate chain-hold (ec2d4b9b) — also
intentional. ONE real, actionable recommendation surfaced: quest-rune-mysteries has by far the highest
downstream fan-out in the bank (22 other bank rows name it in their own reqs.quests — a crude
single-hop proxy, real fan-out is likely higher) and trivial reqs (ready@0), yet carries no
milestone/steer anchor pulling it forward (taken@115) — textbook criterion-#1 "compounding QoL unlock"
that a future ordering pass should consider anchoring early. Runners-up by the same signal:
quest-children-of-the-sun (12), quest-shield-of-arrav (10), rfd-intro (9), quest-creature-of-
fenkenstrain (9), quest-big-chompy (8), quest-underground-pass (7). NOT reordered here — ordering
stays the planner's — flagged for the ordering agent.
Calc cross-check (Experience_table.s2, wikicli-verified): project's own XP_TABLE formula (route_
feasibility.mjs / assets/js/world/xp.js / enrich.py _build_xp_table) matches the live wiki table
EXACTLY at every level checked (15/30/45/60/75/99) — the formula itself is trustworthy. The STORED
`xp` field on train-* bank rows is a different story: 66/120 checked rows mismatch the verified
formula (all level-99 rows share one wrong constant 12862000 vs the real 13034431; other levels show
a scattered pattern consistent with cross-skill/cross-level copy-paste). This is the EXACT issue
gotchas.log's `[training]` line already named ("xp fixture fields are synthetic/wrong for non-level-1
bands") — now quantified. NOT bulk-fixed here (Lane-5 content-authoring scope, and the field is
provably inert: route_feasibility.apply() only folds xp for kind=="quest" rows, never train-*, and
state_scan's skills_delta is computed from grants/effLevel, never this field — so the bad data cannot
leak into feasibility or state_after). MUST-NOT-MISS for Lane 5: recompute every train-*/synth-* `xp`
field from XP_TABLE before ever rendering it player-facing (a `quest-xp` style hint chip, methods xp/hr
comparison, etc.) — the formula is right, the stored numbers are not.
Render (WebFragments.java/app.css/GuideStep.java, runelite-guide-chain): state_after attaches to
GuideStep as field `state_after` (NOT camelCase `stateAfter` — this codebase's convention is the
literal snake_case JSON key as the Java field name, no @SerializedName anywhere; caught this via a
live Gson smoke-parse of route-grand.json before trusting the compile, since compileJava alone can't
catch a field-name/JSON-key mismatch that just silently deserializes to null). Compact "After this →"
chip line, same reused-in-both-contexts placement as paysOff/branch; overlay-only.
MUST-NOT-MISS: state_after is route-POSITION-dependent (same step id at a different route position
would carry different state), so it is NOT portable across routes/re-orders — regenerate the sidecar
(state_scan.mjs <fresh-route> --emit state_after.jsonl) after any change to route-grand's step order,
BEFORE the next enrich pass, or the attached state_after will describe stale positions.
